        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A treadmill stress test records your <strong class="text-white">ECG, blood pressure and
            symptoms</strong> while you walk progressively faster and steeper, usually in
            three-minute Bruce protocol stages. It looks for signs of reduced blood flow to the heart,
            rhythm problems, an unusual blood pressure response and your exercise capacity.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Expect around <strong class="text-white">6 to 15 minutes of walking</strong> inside an
            appointment of about an hour, longer for imaging versions. Wear proper shoes, follow the
            clinic's instructions, and let your clinician explain the result — and if you are later
            cleared to exercise, our
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill workouts</a>
            are a gentle place to start.
          </p>
